      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "Now for the part that varies the most. A landlord cannot sit on your deposit forever. In most US states there is a hard deadline to return it, often within a set number of days after you move out, along with that itemized statement. But the exact clock varies by state. In some places it is around fourteen days, in others closer to thirty, and a few differ again. The only number that matters is the one in your state's law.",
